  "boundaries": [
    "Exact original source is retained; both finite actual-loop lag controls fail by receiving a data frame after the missed batch instead of a close.",
    "Code1013 close is best-effort with a one-second terminal-only grace. The socket is dropped after success, error or timeout; no post-gap stream continuation is allowed.",
    "Existing healthy send backpressure is preserved and can delay observing lag. No new ordinary-send deadline or aggregate resource quota.",
    "Acknowledgement snapshot release is established by explicit source ownership before the await, with content/order/lifetime controls. No allocator or throughput measurement claim.",
    "Five isolated Node controls evaluate actual browser callbacks. This is not a full browser/layout test or a new application/build dependency.",
    "Lost broadcast counts are batches, not rows. Retained history is bounded to10000 notifications and cannot guarantee complete replay; clients must reconcile after continuity loss.",
    "No ingestion write-path or persisted format change, SQL implementation, production data, remote host, live chain or benchmark. Reorg notifications and broader audit acceptance remain open."
  ],
